  "worked_solution": "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply the first equation by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}12.8a+6.4=-6.4b & |\\,\\times 10 \\\\ 2a+1=b & \\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}128a+64=-64b \\\\ 2a+1=b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $b:$\n\n$$\nb=2a+1\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $a,$ we can substitute $b=2a+1$ into the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}128a+64 & =-64b \\\\ 128a+64 & =-64(2a+1) \\\\ 128a+64 & =-128a-64 \\\\ 256a & =-128 \\\\ a & =-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ a & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $a=-0.5$ into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+1 & =b \\\\ 2(-0.5)+1 & =b \\\\ -1+1 & =b \\\\ b & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-0.5$ and $b=0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
